Apple is expanding what <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI can do in and across apps in iOS 27.3, which is available to developers as of today.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051103" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/Siri-AI.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="895" /><br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can complete more complex tasks across Calendar, Files, Finder, Journal, Mail, Maps, Messages, Music, Notes, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a>, Preview, Reminders, Safari, Shortcuts, and Weather. You can ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI what you can do with each app to get more information on what's possible.<br/>
<br/>
In Mail, for example, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can unsubscribe you from mailing lists and undo recently sent messages. In Weather, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can add locations to your weather list, or control weather notifications. In Safari, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can clear browsing history, manage tabs and windows, save articles to a Reading List, and close duplicate tabs. In Files, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can organize content, delete files you haven't accessed for a set period of time, and more.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is also expanding &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI to Traditional Chinese, Vietnamese, Turkish, and Norwegian, and adding a Developer Preview that lets any developer <a href="https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=gdk2umrf">integrate their app</a> with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI.<br/>
<br/>
